{"type":"message","id":"b60fea96","parentId":"31efbfb8","timestamp":"2026-05-28T02:46:54.777Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The POST /send endpoint is returning 500 error with \"error code: 1101\". This seems to be a Cloudflare Workers specific error. The error 1101 is \"Worker threw exception\" - the Cloudflare Worker itself is throwing an exception.\n\nThe GET /history endpoints work fine, but POST /send fails with error 1101. This is likely a bug in the backend, or the endpoint requires different parameters.\n\nLet me try different approaches - maybe the body format is different or the endpoint expects something else.\n","thinkingSignature":"1b0e3c8dbe7b3655b8134e5b37382fbdf5528950fc8f59fbb6f459243e49f802"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_6einv78275hz_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try with different parameter naming\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"message\":\"test\"}' 2>&1","timeout":15}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_6einv78275hz_2","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Check history with POST (which worked earlier) vs send\ncurl -s -X GET \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send?threadId=arbitration\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" 2>&1","timeout":15}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":716,"output":311,"cacheRead":54256,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":55283,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779936404274,"responseId":"0666df9478d4a8c58948d0d85667b9a3"}}
